{
  "$comment": "Response field registry for the fixture (WP-M). render.py passes every record it emits through this map: a field that is not declared here is a build error, so no mock response can carry a field of unknown provenance. 'fields' lists wire names; 'renames' maps a fixture (logical) name to a different wire name if the connector ever renames one (edit here, not in household.json). 'source' is the provenance of the record's field NAMES: captured = seen in the live capture recorded in connector/FIELDS.md (2026-09-22); guide = named in the response guide text but not seen in a payload; assumed = not captured (the tool errored or returned nothing), shaped from the tool description and the build spec, and to be re-checked against the next capture. 'assumed_fields' flags individual assumed fields inside a captured or guide record. Field VALUES in household.json are always synthetic.",
  "version": 1,
  "source": "connector/FIELDS.md (live capture 2026-09-22; names and types only)",
  "records": {
    "envelope": {"source": "captured", "tools": ["*"], "fields": ["data", "guide"]},
    "account": {"source": "captured", "tools": ["get_accounts"], "container": "accounts",
      "fields": ["account_number", "rhs_account_number", "rhc_account_number", "type", "unsettled_funds",
